# Sudoku Arena — Docker build-context exclusions for the PRODUCTION image.
#
# A NEW file at the repository root. `backend/Dockerfile.prod` uses the repository
# root as its build context (it needs both `backend/` and `frontend/`), so this file
# keeps that context small and, more importantly, keeps secrets and local cruft out of
# the image.
#
# This does NOT affect the development stack: Docker reads the `.dockerignore` that
# sits at the root of each build context, and `docker-compose.yml` uses `./backend`
# and `./frontend` as its contexts, neither of which has one. Nothing here changes
# `docker compose up`.

# Secrets — never inside an image layer. The real values come from `.env` at runtime
# through `env_file`, not from the build context.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example

# Version control.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Dependencies: reinstalled inside the image from the lockfile, so a host-side copy
# (possibly built for Windows) must never leak in.
**/node_modules

# Build output: rebuilt inside the image.
**/dist
**/coverage

# Local file storage (BLD-001) — mounted as a volume at runtime, never baked in.
storage
**/storage

# Local scratch and docs that the image does not need.
.claude
.cowork-temp
building-with-ai
testing

# Logs and editor/OS droppings.
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea
.vscode
~$*
